course: dictionary
lesson: 1498
title: Abbreviations in context
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An abbreviation is a short form of a longer name or word. CBC stands for the Canadian Broadcasting Corporation, so three letters are a shortcut. Context helps you work out what the letters stand for.
explain: «When a government controls the TV, it can show only good news about the leader; public broadcasters such as the BBC, ABC or CBC are paid for by the public and meant to report freely.» The sentence lists the BBC, ABC and CBC together, so they must be the same kind of thing: public broadcasters, like TV and radio channels.
explain: The same letters can mean different things in different subjects. In news and TV, CBC is a broadcaster. In medicine, CBC means a blood test. Always ask: what is the topic? Then pick the meaning that fits.
fact: An abbreviation is a shortened form of a word or name, such as CBC.
fact: CBC stands for Canadian Broadcasting Corporation, Canada's public radio and TV broadcaster.
fact: In French, the CBC is called Radio-Canada.
fact: In medicine, CBC means a complete blood count, a common blood test that counts the different kinds of cells in your blood.
fact: Public broadcasters like the BBC in the UK and the ABC in Australia are similar to the CBC.
exercise: In «public broadcasters such as the BBC, ABC or CBC are paid for by the public», what kind of thing is CBC? | A type of bread | A kind of car | *A public radio and TV broadcaster | A blood test
exercise: What does CBC stand for in Canadian news and TV? | Canada Bakery Club | A complete blood count | *Canadian Broadcasting Corporation | Canadian Bike Centre
exercise: A doctor orders a CBC for a sick child. What does CBC mean here? | A radio station in French | *A complete blood count, a common blood test | A kind of bandage | A Canadian children's TV show
test: Why is the phrase «public broadcasters» a useful clue for CBC? | It tells you CBC is a number | It tells you CBC is a type of food | *It tells you CBC is a TV or radio channel paid for by the public | It tells you CBC is a shop
test: Why can the letters CBC mean two different things? | *Because the topic around the word changes what it means | Because dictionaries are out of date | Because CBC is a spelling mistake | Because CBC always means the same thing
exam: What is the best way to work out what an abbreviation like CBC means? | Guess the first answer you think of | Ask someone else to read it for you without thinking | *Read the topic and the words around it, then check a dictionary if you are unsure | Skip the whole text and never come back
